        <name>timerCallback</name>
        <qualifiedname>nexus::Link::ConnectTimer::timerCallback</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Periodic retry callback fired every 100 ms by the JUCE timer. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each tick reads the port from the <computeroutput>.<ref refid="namespacenexus" kindref="compound">nexus</ref></computeroutput> file on disk and attempts <computeroutput>connectToSocket</computeroutput>. Reading from disk rather than <ref refid="struct_app_model" kindref="compound">AppModel</ref> in-memory means the timer can succeed on the very first tick that the daemon has written its port file, even before <ref refid="struct_app_model" kindref="compound">AppModel</ref> has been updated. On success the timer stops itself; JUCE will fire <computeroutput><ref refid="classnexus_1_1_link_1a38af409bc1c85a1faf8636e8ba297987" kindref="member">Link::connectionMade</ref></computeroutput>. On exhaustion the timer stops and a failure line is logged.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>NEXUS PROCESS MESSAGE THREAD. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
